  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Machines.** `assets/machines/makera-carvera.mch` and `makera-carvera-air.mch` are new, registered in `posting::MACHINES`. The figures come from the \"Specs\" tables on Makera's own product pages (read 2026-11-10):\n\n| | Carvera (C1) | Carvera Air |\n|---|---|---|\n| Work area (mm), as ±stroke | 360 × 240 × 140 | 300 × 200 × 130 |\n| Spindle | 200 W, to 15000 rpm | 200 W, to 13000 rpm |\n| Axis feed and rapid | 6000 mm/min | 4000 mm/min |\n| Tool changer | 6 | none stated (quick changer) |\n| Coolant | Air (M7) | Air (M7) |\n\nNo `min_speed` is stated, because Makera publishes \"0 – 15000 rpm\" and the validator refuses 0. The optional 4th-axis module is left out; it's a later step.\n\n**Post.** `assets/posts/carvera.cps` is registered as \"Makera Carvera\". It writes only words from the firmware's supported-codes tables (Smoothieware-based).\n\n| Area | What it writes |\n|---|---|\n| Header | `G21 G17 G90 G94`. An inch machine is refused by name, because G20 halts the firmware. |\n| Tool change | `M6 Tn`. There's no G43, because the firmware measures tool length itself. Tool 0 (the wireless probe) is refused as a cutter. |\n| Spindle and air | `M3 S…`, then the machine's M7 air, off with M9. |\n| Arcs | `G2`/`G3` with relative I/J/K, in G17, G18 or G19. |\n| Drilling | No canned cycles in the firmware, so drilling posts as its expanded chain, with `G4 P<s>` dwells at the hole bottom. |\n| Program end | `M2`, because M30 does nothing on a Carvera. |\n| Refused by name | tapping, control cutter compensation, tilted moves and probe operations. |\n\n`docs/decisions/707-carvera.md` records every choice and its source.\n\n## Pinned by\n\n- **`carvera_machines`:** `every_carvera_states_makeras_figures`.\n- **`carvera_post`:**\n  - `a_two_tool_pocket_posts_in_the_carveras_own_words` locks the golden `golden/nc/carvera/two_tool_pocket.nc` on the shipped C1 file and asserts no G43 / G49 / G40 / G80 / G91.1 / G20 / M8 / M30 / G53;\n  - `an_inch_machine_is_refused_by_name`;\n  - `tool_zero_is_the_probe_and_refused_as_a_cutter`;\n  - `control_cutter_compensation_is_refused_by_name`.\n- **`conformance`:** the Carvera on every mill golden (`golden/nc/carvera/`), with `tap_plate` refused by name; the synth stream (`synth_carvera.nc`); and the extension pin.\n- **`machine`:** the shipped-machine list.\n\n## How tested\n\nOn upstream main plus this branch:\n- every `camcraft-app` test suite and `--lib` pass. `lathe_thread_travel` was left out because it doesn't build on main (#686). The `probe_dialects` fix (#700) has already merged.\n- clippy `-D warnings` is clean on the app lib and the touched tests.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThere has been no run on a real Carvera or in Carvera Controller. I'm asking a contributor with the machine to run `two_tool_pocket.nc` before the post is trusted on a machine. The fork is synced at v0.16.0; the branch is cut from upstream/main for the current machine registry.\n\nChangelog: Makera Carvera and Carvera Air machines, and a Carvera post that speaks the Carvera firmware (#707)\n\nFixes #707\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
